<%#
  Miscellaneous settings. A page of subtabs rather than a growing row of
  top-level tabs, so small preferences have somewhere to live without each one
  claiming a tab of its own.
%>
<div id="miscSettings">
  <%# Sub-TABS, not pills: pills read as buttons, and these select a page of
      settings the way the tabs above them do. %>
  <ul class="nav nav-tabs mb-3" id="miscSubTabs" role="tablist">
    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
      <button class="nav-link active" type="button" role="tab" data-misc-tab="focus-colours">
        <i class="bi bi-palette2"></i> Focus colours
      </button>
    </li>
    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
      <button class="nav-link" type="button" role="tab" data-misc-tab="status-digest">
        <i class="bi bi-envelope-paper"></i> Status digest
      </button>
    </li>
    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
      <button class="nav-link" type="button" role="tab" data-misc-tab="focus-monitors">
        <i class="bi bi-grid-3x3-gap"></i> Focus monitors
      </button>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="misc-subpane" data-misc-pane="focus-colours">
    <p class="text-muted small">
      The colours offered when you right-click an item on the focus bar. Give each
      one a name so the menu says what it means - "Blocked" reads better than a
      swatch you have to remember. Stored in this browser, like the theme.
    </p>

    <table class="table table-sm align-middle" style="max-width: 34rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="width: 4rem;">Colour</th>
          <th>Means</th>
          <th style="width: 3rem;"></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody id="focusColourRows"></tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="btn-group" role="group" style="display: inline-flex; gap: 2px;">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" id="addFocusColourBtn">+ Colour</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" id="saveFocusColoursBtn">Save</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" id="resetFocusColoursBtn">Reset to defaults</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="misc-subpane" data-misc-pane="status-digest" hidden>
    <p class="text-muted small">
      The update to management, written for you on a schedule. Nothing is sent:
      the app holds no mail credentials, and sending on your behalf by surprise
      is not a thing it should do - so the digest is written, kept here, and
      handed to your mail client when you press send.
    </p>

    <div class="row g-2 align-items-end" style="max-width: 40rem;">
      <div class="col-auto">
        <div class="form-check form-switch">
          <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="digestEnabled">
          <label class="form-check-label" for="digestEnabled">Write one on a schedule</label>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-auto">
        <label class="form-label small mb-0" for="digestDay">Every</label>
        <select class="form-select form-select-sm" id="digestDay">
          <option value="1">Monday</option>
          <option value="2">Tuesday</option>
          <option value="3">Wednesday</option>
          <option value="4">Thursday</option>
          <option value="5">Friday</option>
          <option value="6">Saturday</option>
          <option value="0">Sunday</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="col-auto">
        <label class="form-label small mb-0" for="digestTime">at</label>
        <input type="time" class="form-control form-control-sm" id="digestTime" value="16:00">
      </div>
      <div class="col-auto">
        <label class="form-label small mb-0" for="digestDays">covering the last</label>
        <div class="input-group input-group-sm">
          <input type="number" class="form-control" id="digestDays" min="1" max="90" value="7">
          <span class="input-group-text">days</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="btn-group mt-3" role="group" style="display: inline-flex; gap: 2px;">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" id="saveDigestBtn">Save schedule</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" id="runDigestBtn">Write one now</button>
    </div>

    <div id="digestPreview" class="mt-3" hidden>
      <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-1">
        <strong id="digestSubject"></strong>
        <span class="text-muted small" id="digestWhen"></span>
      </div>
      <textarea id="digestBody" class="form-control" rows="14" readonly></textarea>
      <div class="btn-group mt-2" role="group" style="display: inline-flex; gap: 2px;">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" id="copyDigestBtn">Copy</button>
        <a class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" id="mailDigestBtn" href="#">Open in mail client</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="misc-subpane" data-misc-pane="focus-monitors" hidden>
    <p class="text-muted small">
      The pin bar can be split into any number of "monitors" - black squares you drag
      pinned items onto and between. Each one can carry an optional label and
      choose whether its items sit side by side or stack with only the top one
      showing until you click it open.
    </p>

    <div class="row g-2 align-items-end" style="max-width: 40rem;">
      <div class="col-auto">
        <label class="form-label small mb-0" for="monitorCount">Number of monitors</label>
        <%# 0 is a real choice: with no monitors the focus bar is not drawn at
            all. Pins are kept, not discarded - set a monitor back and they
            reappear where they were. `max` is filled in from the server's own
            bound when the settings load, so this markup never has to know it. %>
        <input type="number" class="form-control form-control-sm" id="monitorCount"
               min="0" step="1" style="width: 7rem;"
               aria-describedby="monitorCountHelp">
        <div class="form-text small" id="monitorCountHelp">0 hides the bar</div>
      </div>
      <div class="col-auto">
        <div class="form-check form-switch">
          <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="monitorShowNumbers">
          <label class="form-check-label" for="monitorShowNumbers">Show monitor numbers</label>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <table class="table table-sm align-middle mt-3" style="max-width: 40rem;">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="width: 3rem;">#</th>
          <th>Label (optional)</th>
          <th style="width: 14rem;">Layout</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody id="monitorRows"></tbody>
    </table>

    <div class="btn-group" role="group" style="display: inline-flex; gap: 2px;">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" id="saveMonitorsBtn">Save</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script src="/js/settings-misc.js"></script>
